#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124197 :question/id #uuid "35a664b8-a895-5c52-a92f-b62c75b44744" :question/math-academy-id "e-11026" :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$ given that $f(x,y) = 3x\\ln y + 2ye^x.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+2y{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =3x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)+2{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\  & =3x\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}+2{e}^{x}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{3x}{y}+2{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124201 :question/id #uuid "a14d53ae-1922-531d-bb2a-bda9b4829f6e" :question/math-academy-id "e-11045" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y) = y^2\\ln{x},$ express $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ as the limit of a difference quotient." :question/worked-solution "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} = \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\left(\\dfrac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x) = y^2 \\ln{x},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x+h,y) = y^2\\ln(x+h).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} = \\lim_{h \\to 0}\\left( \\dfrac{y^2\\ln(x+h) -y^2\\ln{x} }{h}\\right).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124202 :question/id #uuid "ee2294e1-1e9a-5be5-be47-4c2e295b640a" :question/math-academy-id "e-11049" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y) = x^2y^2+\\sin{x}\\cos{y},$ evaluate $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ at the point $(\\pi,2\\pi).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\cdot (2x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =2x{y}^{2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\pi,2\\pi)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(\\pi ,2\\pi )} & =2\\cdot \\pi \\cdot (2\\pi )^{2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi  \\\\  & =2\\pi \\cdot 4{\\pi }^{2}+(-1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =8{\\pi }^{3}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124786 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf04fd45-6472-58ca-94d4-d15d2e211452" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy - x^{2}\\sin y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121314} {:answer/id #uuid "e86f2714-6951-57a6-9a39-8cf927f5a779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y - \\sin y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121315} {:answer/id #uuid "f1c60716-d08f-5601-a61d-2122e60c3f07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{2} + 2x\\sin y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121316} {:answer/id #uuid "f9c2f3ce-5cce-5e2c-9e3f-2b7a5ddf7527" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{2} - 2x\\sin y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121317} {:answer/id #uuid "5027f72a-8193-5afe-a1d0-c7fc0aa88343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy + x^{2}\\sin y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121318}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ea625c07-3c2c-5ede-a249-984720aa8ae8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/