_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{3(x+h)^{2}y-3{x}^{2}y}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436294} {:answer/id #uuid "a0c460cb-67db-5572-99a9-ee900ea57026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{3{x}^{2}y-3{x}^{2}(y+h)}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436309} {:answer/id #uuid "cf081fa8-128f-5e46-8325-e879a6351185" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{3{x}^{2}(y+h)+3{x}^{2}y}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436315} {:answer/id #uuid "d91afb82-9ea2-57cb-beea-4efb7de3116e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{3(x+h)^{2}y+3{x}^{2}y}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436316} {:answer/id #uuid "e544a325-ec37-5b38-a930-60dd700bae41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{3{x}^{2}(y+h)-3{x}^{2}y}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a982a06-37f5-5503-bfa9-cb1dd6d38914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{3(x+h)^{2}y-3{x}^{2}y}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436294} :answer-field/id #uuid "55b7ddca-7b00-5c43-89e9-90f57dc02219" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121433}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b1789afc-331e-5614-8cc9-89f93ec40167" :question/math-academy-id "q-158412" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}y,$ then $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=3{x}^{2}y$,  we have that \n\n$$\nf(