/id #uuid "31f0a8fb-fb91-5f05-a1c6-0f7919bcc8ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560265} {:answer/id #uuid "61d1bf7e-2e8a-58b1-89e7-37532ce1d411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560275} {:answer/id #uuid "c650800f-fc8f-5c0f-87af-deec9d5ecc1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560284} {:answer/id #uuid "ca25a9be-e802-5e45-a463-cc3c224d6a15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca25a9be-e802-5e45-a463-cc3c224d6a15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560286} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4dd3c96-722f-59d8-a3ad-81a44cf6e35a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c63a6c19-50b5-5979-ba7a-341fdd52675a" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=x \\sec{(y )}+y x^{4},$ evaluate ${f}_{y}(- \\sqrt{2},\\frac{\\pi}{4}).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x \\sec{(y )}+y x^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x \\sec{(y )})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y x^{4}) \\\\  & =x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sec{(y )})+x^{4}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\  & =x\\cdot (\\sec{(y )} \\tan{(y )})+x^{4}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =x \\sec{(y )} \\tan{(y )}+x^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(- \\sqrt{2},\\frac{\\pi}{4}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(- \\sqrt{2},\\frac{\\pi}{4}) & =(- \\sqrt{2}) \\sec{(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) )} \\tan{(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) )}+(- \\sqrt{2})^{4} \\\\  & =(- \\sqrt{2})\\cdot (\\sqrt{2})\\cdot (1)+(4) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560287 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29a08cee-ed02-5faf-a682-255c5139e134" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560262} {:answer/id #uuid "45f467e8-e600-5a7b-8133-7812e4904ae9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560271} {:answer/id #uuid "dd410a64-adab-5eb3-b6b4-3a9d9d8cdef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560290} {:answer/id #uuid "e55c0a40-c359-5478-8e4c-9a627191e993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560294} {:answer/id #uuid "fdee8958-2bb7-5874-bfe6-048f32451748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd410a64-adab-5eb3-b6b4-3a9d9d8cdef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560290} :answer-field/id #uuid "26db9502-5c6f-59a9-b551-456ea58a9398" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560260}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cf3c77be-ed81-5de6-b0a0-3c22ecd64ed6" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=3 y^{2} x^{2}+y x,$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3 y^{2} x^{2}+y x) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3 y^{2} x^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y x) \\\\  & =3 x^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y^{2})+x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\  & =3 x^{2}\\cdot (2 y)+x\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =6 y x^{2}+x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(1,-1)} & =6 (-1) (1)^{2}+(1) \\\\  & =-6+(1) \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560292 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "019ef7fd-1e40-5bfa-b396-c65b7986b509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560257} {:answer/id #uuid "879a6590-6d16-5057-9f9b-f643a19b8efc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560281} {:answer/id #uuid "da8bb81f-1925-585b-8a5a-bc3432ec5ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560289} {:answer/id #uuid "eda61f1e-52c0-529f-87ce-9712ea47c7f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560295} {:answer/id #uuid "f1342a2b-1459-59d2-89f7-1a0aff24bc4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "019ef7fd-1e40-5bfa-b396-c65b7986b509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560257} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cb4fff8-45ad-50c3-8b2e-9b437dd13890" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560273}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e2c0e388-7239-552d-8839-6c9035d1a779" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=3 y^{2} x^{2}+2 y x,$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3 y^{2} x^{2}+2 y x) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3 y^{2} x^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2 y x) \\\\  & =3 x^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y^{2})+2 x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\  & =3 x^{2}\\cdot (2 y)+2 x\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =6 y x^{2}+2 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(1,1)} & =6 (1) (1)^{2}+2 (1) \\\\  & =6+(2) \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560297 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ea927af-1007-572a-922f-4aefb0c8767e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560264} {:answer/id #uuid "61615a5c-1c97-5ca0-97b9-f795b28e5c8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560274} {:answer/id #uuid "64686f40-7ee7-549c-8a01-588a18b5d8b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560276} {:answer/id #uuid "7176a7f5-da12-53cf-9ffd-85f92b2fb510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560279} {:answer/id #uuid "e1c4d2a1-1c92-5c12-9540-6b62a7ee553f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ea927af-1007-572a-922f-4aefb0c8767e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560264} :answer-field/id #uuid "371473f6-d498-5af3-980f-2a37043ccdd6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560268}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f71f04b5-8161-5a16-8003-15968bea5986" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=3 x^{2} y^{2}+x y,$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(-2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3 x^{2} y^{2}+x y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3 x^{2} y^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x y) \\\\  & =3 y^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2})+y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\  & =3 y^{2}\\cdot (2 x)+y\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =6 x y^{2}+y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(-2,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(-2,1)} & =6 (-2) (1)^{2}+(1) \\\\  & =-12+(1) \\\\  & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562819 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f5e0c12-1df1-526a-96c6-ab0dd18cf612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-2(1)^{2}(1+h))-(-2(1)^{2}(1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562817} {:answer/id #uuid "54dcebd4-5b21-52a1-abea-45e80438c3b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-2(1+h)^{2}(1))-(-2(1)^{2}(1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562828} {:answer/id #uuid "632579ce-df9a-5c03-80b6-219fd7dfc7c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-2(1)^{2}(1))-(-2(1+h)^{2}(1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562830} {:answer/id #uuid "9fcbe737-7d67-54f0-a0af-c34445d7c218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-2(1+h)^{2}(1+h))-(-2(1)^{2}(1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562837} {:answer/id #uuid "aabfb2a7-9bda-52fd-af6a-cdfe4ba02cbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-2(1+h)^{2}(1))+(-2(1)^{2}(1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562838}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54dcebd4-5b21-52a1-abea-45e80438c3b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-2(1+h)^{2}(1))-(-2(1)^{2}(1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562828} :answer-field/id #uuid "68616b5a-bbb9-56c3-8c1b-bdbfac656417" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562833}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "133d6a6b-ec9d-5351-abbd-509a18e66f7b" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=-2{y}^{2}x,$ express $f_y(1,1)$ as the limit of a difference quotient." :question/worked-solution "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by the limit\n\n$$\nf_y(1,1)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{f(1, 1+h)-f(1,1)}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x,y)=-2{y}^{2}x,$ we have that\n\n$$\nf(1, 1+h)=-2(1+h)^{2}(1),\\qquad f(1,1)=-2(1)^{2}(1).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf_y(1,1)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-2(1+h)^{2}(1))-(-2(1)^{2}(1))}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nHere $h\\ne 0$ before taking the limit, and $x=1$ is held constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562824 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f6c1947-d835-5c18-a01c-a8f81e230e0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-3(-2)^{2}(-2+h))-(-3(-2)^{2}(-2))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562822} {:answer/id #uuid "65c76a03-53cd-5585-99f3-7193eb83af98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-3(-2+h)^{2}(-2+h))-(-3(-2)^{2}(-2))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562831} {:answer/id #uuid "6609cbc2-741d-54fb-ac98-8aebd8de56e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-3(-2+h)^{2}(-2))-(-3(-2)^{2}(-2))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562832} {:answer/id #uuid "b0aae4cc-928f-57bf-8b77-9a2911c3a705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-3(-2)^{2}(-2))-(-3(-2+h)^{2}(-2))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562840} {:answer/id #uuid "ed53f686-6565-5dc4-b9f1-ccc38b09f217" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-3(-2+h)^{2}(-2))+(-3(-2)^{2}(-2))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6609cbc2-741d-54fb-ac98-8aebd8de56e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-3(-2+h)^{2}(-2))-(-3(-2)^{2}(-2))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562832} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cae743a-d164-5395-a90d-ce6590411561" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "33532890-70b2-5090-87ea-44260978f50e" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=-3{x}^{2}y,$ express $f_x(-2,-2)$ as the limit of a difference quotient." :question/worked-solution "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit\n\n$$\nf_x(-2,-2)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{f(-2+h, -2)-f(-2,-2)}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x,y)=-3{x}^{2}y,$ we have that\n\n$$\nf(-2+h, -2)=-3(-2+h)^{2}(-2),\\qquad f(-2,-2)=-3(-2)^{2}(-2).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf_x(-2,-2)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(-3(-2+h)^{2}(-2))-(-3(-2)^{2}(-2))}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nHere $h\\ne 0$ before taking the limit, and $y=-2$ is held constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562826 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10ded65f-6e9b-5abc-af2a-f6ea15ffbc0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(-1+h)^{2}(-1+h))-(1(-1)^{2}(-1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562818} {:answer/id #uuid "1c3853fb-b9f6-5eb0-8abe-3badc14e5532" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(-1+h)^{2}(-1))-(1(-1)^{2}(-1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562821} {:answer/id #uuid "5c39a581-ebf6-5756-a15b-ee8d27855840" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(-1)^{2}(-1))-(1(-1+h)^{2}(-1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562829} {:answer/id #uuid "d02c0bbd-88f0-558c-ace0-1036b9f87d32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(-1+h)^{2}(-1))+(1(-1)^{2}(-1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562845} {:answer/id #uuid "f47c17a0-6a4a-5ef5-bdcd-1970900507b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(-1)^{2}(-1+h))-(1(-1)^{2}(-1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c3853fb-b9f6-5eb0-8abe-3badc14e5532" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(-1+h)^{2}(-1))-(1(-1)^{2}(-1))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562821} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c86581d-680b-586d-acbc-3448ad4ff62a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4ab0bfc6-d8ee-5e0d-9b62-1ad460fd0c69" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=1{x}^{2}y,$ express $f_x(-1,-1)$ as the limit of a difference quotient." :question/worked-solution "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit\n\n$$\nf_x(-1,-1)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{f(-1+h, -1)-f(-1,-1)}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x,y)=1{x}^{2}y,$ we have that\n\n$$\nf(-1+h, -1)=1(-1+h)^{2}(-1),\\qquad f(-1,-1)=1(-1)^{2}(-1).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf_x(-1,-1)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(-1+h)^{2}(-1))-(1(-1)^{2}(-1))}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nHere $h\\ne 0$ before taking the limit, and $y=-1$ is held constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562835 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "142263e2-ffc1-5971-aab7-a78e8fb89d3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}((2+h)(3)))-(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562820} {:answer/id #uuid "3882cc29-e493-5280-8251-94acc6ea11be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}((2+h)(3+h)))-(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562825} {:answer/id #uuid "6b6269b9-5085-5358-b7f7-9136abf836c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}((2+h)(3)))+(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562834} {:answer/id #uuid "cc0c1ad0-0809-5caa-abd0-3c394f9b2ffc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3+h)))-(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562844} {:answer/id #uuid "d6d16f5b-c575-532b-8e3a-633aa682efa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)))-(\\operatorname{sin}((2+h)(3)))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "142263e2-ffc1-5971-aab7-a78e8fb89d3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}((2+h)(3)))-(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562820} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0a173b9-7073-5910-96e4-56dae5d5791d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562842}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "77fe6685-0db5-512c-a146-7a7385d90d5f" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}(xy),$ express $f_x(2,3)$ as the limit of a difference quotient." :question/worked-solution "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit\n\n$$\nf_x(2,3)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{f(2+h, 3)-f(2,3)}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}(xy),$ we have that\n\n$$\nf(2+h, 3)=\\operatorname{sin}((2+h)(3)),\\qquad f(2,3)=\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf_x(2,3)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}((2+h)(3)))-(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)))}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nHere $h\\ne 0$ before taking the limit, and $y=3$ is held constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562843 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d025d8c-206e-577a-a3ad-a8da0363314c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(1)^{2}(2+h))-(1(1)^{2}(2))}{h}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592