$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf_x(1,2)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\left(\\frac{(1(1+h)^{2}(2))-(1(1)^{2}(2))}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nHere $h\\ne 0$ before taking the limit, and $y=2$ is held constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563918 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bdec8d3-0363-5eab-8216-e13c1bc6dfc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32 y^{3} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 4 \\arctan{\\left(x \\right)} - \\frac{2 y}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563913} {:answer/id #uuid "3fde6af7-e556-5f3d-be08-5a96003cbd72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 y^{4} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{4 y}{x^{2} + 1} - \\frac{2 y^{2}}{x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563920} {:answer/id #uuid "7b18f342-7832-5070-80b5-ac6287b1e6ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 y^{4} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{4}{x^{2} + 1} + \\frac{2 y^{2}}{x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563932} {:answer/id #uuid "f0d2d702-1a45-5763-80bf-ddbc0c8e01fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 y^{4} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{4 y}{x^{2} + 1} + \\frac{2 y^{2}}{x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563943} {:answer/id #uuid "fb8bd3bb-d891-5b48-b7c5-d72caa5b2b4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 y^{4} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{4 y}{x^{2} + 1} + \\frac{2 y^{2}}{x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0d2d702-1a45-5763-80bf-ddbc0c8e01fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 y^{4} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{4 y}{x^{2} + 1} + \\frac{2 y^{2}}{x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563943} :answer-field/id #uuid "76582032-af87-5d6f-82c4-522f1be624eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563929}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "358908ba-e0d7-5631-bfea-bfcff1b40f32" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ for $$\n\\displaystyle f(x,y)=8 y^{4} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}+4 y \\arctan{\\left(x \\right)}- \\frac{y^{2}}{x^{2}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The notation ${f}_{x}$ denotes the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x.$\n\nWe differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8 y^{4} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}+4 y \\arctan{\\left(x \\right)}- \\frac{y^{2}}{x^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8 y^{4} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4 y \\arctan{\\left(x \\right)})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{y^{2}}{x^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =8 y^{4}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})+4 y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\arctan{\\left(x \\right)})-y^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{1}{x^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =8 y^{4}\\cdot \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}+4 y\\cdot \\frac{1}{x^{2} + 1}-y^{2}\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{2}{x^{3}}\\right) \\\\  & =8 y^{4} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{4 y}{x^{2} + 1} + \\frac{2 y^{2}}{x^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563923 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68032335-7ad1-5905-be82-d1352bbfb651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 x^{4}}{y} - \\frac{18 x^{2}}{y^{3}} + 2 x e^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563925} {:answer/id #uuid "6b97efc7-96e6-548d-9747-5cffdc532dc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 x^{4}}{y} + \\frac{18 x^{2}}{y^{3}} + 2 x e^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563926} {:answer/id #uuid "6bc357a2-4d8d-5bb5-83bb-a1d6124f6d08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 x^{4}}{y} + \\frac{18 x^{2}}{y^{3}} + 2 e^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563927} {:answer/id #uuid "78b438d2-03af-5ea4-b2a1-c55529c78830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 x^{3} \\ln{\\left(y \\right)} - \\frac{18 x}{y^{2}} + 2 e^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563930} {:answer/id #uuid "9d4cc921-f6e2-523b-81f3-c30c21971313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 x^{4} \\ln{\\left(y \\right)} + \\frac{18 x^{2}}{y^{3}} + 2 x e^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563936}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b97efc7-96e6-548d-9747-5cffdc532dc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 x^{4}}{y} + \\frac{18 x^{2}}{y^{3}} + 2 x e^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563926} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d5a7b03-c824-563d-a453-efaa5a4681b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563916}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "53c46985-75bd-5d0e-8acf-681defd4e494" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=3 x^{4} \\ln{\\left(y \\right)}+2 x e^{y}- \\frac{9 x^{2}}{y^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "The notation ${f}_{y}$ denotes the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y.$\n\nWe differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3 x^{4} \\ln{\\left(y \\right)}+2 x e^{y}- \\frac{9 x^{2}}{y^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3 x^{4} \\ln{\\left(y \\right)})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2 x e^{y})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\left(\\frac{9 x^{2}}{y^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =3 x^{4}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\ln{\\left(y \\right)})+2 x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(e^{y})-9 x^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}\\left(\\frac{1}{y^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =3 x^{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}+2 x\\cdot e^{y}-9 x^{2}\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{2}{y^{3}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{3 x^{4}}{y} + \\frac{18 x^{2}}{y^{3}} + 2 x e^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563935 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e86ebca-d073-5614-920c-2c40368c5855" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9 x^{4}}{y} - \\frac{24 x^{2}}{y^{5}} + 6 x e^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563922} {:answer/id #uuid "5e528259-2bf2-593c-ad87-b336511c725f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36 x^{3} \\ln{\\left(y \\right)} - \\frac{12 x}{y^{4}} + 6 e^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563924} {:answer/id #uuid "86904204-2b1a-5604-96a0-fe1dacd76618" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9 x^{4}}{y} + \\frac{24 x^{2}}{y^{5}} + 6 e^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563933} {:answer/id #uuid "ad0ad5bb-cac7-5166-853a-00283b9beefc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 x^{4} \\ln{\\left(y \\right)} + \\frac{24 x^{2}}{y^{5}} + 6 x e^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563937} {:answer/id #uuid "da58126b-9127-5f9d-9267-f655f93757b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9 x^{4}}{y} + \\frac{24 x^{2}}{y^{5}} + 6 x e^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da58126b-9127-5f9d-9267-f655f93757b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9 x^{4}}{y} + \\frac{24 x^{2}}{y^{5}} + 6 x e^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563942} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ce72965-2dc9-57f6-9a7b-6bd0fd9851ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563911}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9b8b664b-9453-5df3-adfd-d88aab5ec4b9" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=9 x^{4} \\ln{\\left(y \\right)}+6 x e^{y}- \\frac{6 x^{2}}{y^{4}}.$" :question/worked-solution "The notation ${f}_{y}$ denotes the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y.$\n\nWe differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(9 x^{4} \\ln{\\left(y \\right)}+6 x e^{y}- \\frac{6 x^{2}}{y^{4}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(9 x^{4} \\ln{\\left(y \\right)})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(6 x e^{y})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\left(\\frac{6 x^{2}}{y^{4}}\\right) \\\\  & =9 x^{4}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\ln{\\left(y \\right)})+6 x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(e^{y})-6 x^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}\\left(\\frac{1}{y^{4}}\\right) \\\\  & =9 x^{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}+6 x\\cdot e^{y}-6 x^{2}\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{4}{y^{5}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{9 x^{4}}{y} + \\frac{24 x^{2}}{y^{5}} + 6 x e^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563938 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "299bed61-393a-57ef-bc40-e403263bea41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 y e^{x} + \\frac{3 y^{4}}{x} + \\frac{2 y^{2}}{x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563915} {:answer/id #uuid "34a0345d-a500-541a-9f3d-382c91bbe4fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 y^{3} \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} + 4 e^{x} - \\frac{2 y}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563917} {:answer/id #uuid "3addf247-3600-5696-a597-18ce1d4fe1a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 y e^{x} + \\frac{3 y^{4}}{x} - \\frac{2 y^{2}}{x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563919} {:answer/id #uuid "74a37371-78a7-5f96-a731-2d709ec5223c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 e^{x} + \\frac{3 y^{4}}{x} + \\frac{2 y^{2}}{x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563928} {:answer/id #uuid "79b0c26f-a5e2-52d4-96e9-f00d28e2adb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 y^{4} \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} + 4 y e^{x} + \\frac{2 y^{2}}{x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "299bed61-393a-57ef-bc40-e403263bea41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 y e^{x} + \\frac{3 y^{4}}{x} + \\frac{2 y^{2}}{x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563915} :answer-field/id #uuid "c86626fa-9415-5008-93eb-9d025f49dc63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563941}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b3b331d0-9e79-50ba-986a-26001df1f72a" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=3 y^{4} \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}+4 y e^{x}- \\frac{y^{2}}{x^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "The notation ${f}_{x}$ denotes the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x.$\n\nWe differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3 y^{4} \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}+4 y e^{x}- \\frac{y^{2}}{x^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3 y^{4} \\ln{\\left(x \\right)})+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4 y e^{x})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{y^{2}}{x^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =3 y^{4}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\ln{\\left(x \\right)})+4 y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(e^{x})-y^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{1}{x^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =3 y^{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}+4 y\\cdot e^{x}-y^{2}\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{2}{x^{3}}\\right) \\\\  & =4 y e^{x} + \\frac{3 y^{4}}{x} + \\frac{2 y^{2}}{x^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563939 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c8f599d-831f-5be1-a7f2-eb934263746c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 x^{4} \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} + \\frac{9 x^{2}}{y^{4}} + \\frac{9}{y^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563910} {:answer/id #uuid "23db01ce-0748-517a-a55b-f582e03db432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32 x^{3} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} - \\frac{6 x}{y^{3}} + 9 \\arctan{\\left(y \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563914} {:answer/id #uuid "43a148d3-9892-5fd6-af0e-5e2de55e18bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 x^{4} \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} + \\frac{9 x^{2}}{y^{4}} + \\frac{9 x}{y^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563921} {:answer/id #uuid "913ea125-5439-59c9-937d-f47f89923df9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 x^{4} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + \\frac{9 x^{2}}{y^{4}} + \\frac{9 x}{y^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563934} {:answer/id #uuid "b76686c0-e762-51a7-9a52-4022ee86fe5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 x^{4} \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - \\frac{9 x^{2}}{y^{4}} + \\frac{9 x}{y^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43a148d3-9892-5fd6-af0e-5e2de55e18bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 x^{4} \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} + \\frac{9 x^{2}}{y^{4}} + \\frac{9 x}{y^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563921} :answer-field/id #uuid "1656178c-d374-56ef-bdd1-26d275bae562" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563912}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b43704d0-6be6-52a5-b0ab-6873dc76da8f" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ for $$\n\\displaystyle f(x,y)=8 x^{4} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}+9 x \\arctan{\\left(y \\right)}- \\frac{3 x^{2}}{y^{3}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The notation ${f}_{y}$ denotes the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y.$\n\nWe differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(8 x^{4} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}+9 x \\arctan{\\left(y \\right)}- \\frac{3 x^{2}}{y^{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(8 x^{4} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(9 x \\arctan{\\left(y \\right)})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\left(\\frac{3 x^{2}}{y^{3}}\\right) \\\\  & =8 x^{4}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sin{\\left(y \\right)})+9 x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\arctan{\\left(y \\right)})-3 x^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}\\left(\\frac{1}{y^{3}}\\right) \\\\  & =8 x^{4}\\cdot \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}+9 x\\cdot \\frac{1}{y^{2} + 1}-3 x^{2}\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{3}{y^{4}}\\right) \\\\  & =8 x^{4} \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} + \\frac{9 x^{2}}{y^{4}} + \\frac{9 x}{y^{2} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712881 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06308084-f04f-5090-a6f4-dd6060453a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712871} {:answer/id #uuid "14e59890-4537-539d-b6fc-ff850eb4b3ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712875} {:answer/id #uuid "2b1bc1bf-d3ca-5ef6-95b7-232e988ce093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712878} {:answer/id #uuid "693711ce-f4b2-59ed-acf8-f6c94c65b436" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712884} {:answer/id #uuid "ac899296-7aad-5d7e-a301-0ccc2faa4594" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06308084-f04f-5090-a6f4-dd6060453a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712871} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6510e5a-1b86-5bd8-87f9-467d5ff85b2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "54f4d22d-a239-5fcb-afa5-eee103469884" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=x^2y+y^3$, evaluate $f_x(2,3)$.\n\nTreat $y$ as a constant when differentiating with respect to $x$." :question/worked-solution "Hold $y$ fixed. The factor $y$ in $x^2y$ is constant, and the entire term $y^3$ is constant with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x(x,y)&=y\\frac{d}{dx}(x^2)+\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(y^3)\\\\\n&=y(2x)+0\\\\\n&=2xy.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow substitute the coordinates into the derivative:\n\n$$\nf_x(2,3)=2\\cdot2\\cdot3=12.\n$$\n\nThe requested value is a derivative value, rather than the function value $f(2,3)=39$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712886 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11a852a4-0a69-55ed-8493-76cf63e4cddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712873} {:answer/id #uuid "3d34b0ad-a4d4-5ec4-83fe-9ce7625d8328" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712879} {:answer/id #uuid "46717083-3ffb-584a-a9a0-063b0c06f24c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712880} {:answer/id #uuid "7f65060f-5112-5914-9f08-b8e78ec33a4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712885} {:answer/id #uuid "95637d02-e879-5b64-90ff-74a4a5945e62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46717083-3ffb-584a-a9a0-063b0c06f24c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712880} :answer-field/id #uuid "09829f4f-95be-53fa-a7c9-b1a5f8e86c0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712872}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "806fd5f6-6859-5b61-b789-17ba59235429" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=y^2\\sqrt{x}+\\frac{x}{y}$, evaluate $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$ at the point $(9,3)$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate with respect to $y$, holding $x$ fixed. In particular, $\\sqrt{x}$ and $x$ are constant factors. Rewrite the reciprocal as a negative power:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_y(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(y^2\\sqrt{x}+xy^{-1}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{x}(2y)+x(-y^{-2})\\\\\n&=2y\\sqrt{x}-\\frac{x}{y^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate both contributions at $(9,3)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_y(9,3)&=2\\cdot3\\cdot\\sqrt{9}-\\frac{9}{3^2}\\\\\n&=18-1\\\\\n&=17.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712888 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "132fe52c-77a0-545d-8cf3-d20c12b04079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712874} {:answer/id #uuid "1f7da2fb-1a07-530a-b156-87159f2af2f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712876} {:answer/id #uuid "551c7c6e-6e0b-58c9-b3c9-5024b1b3d3c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712882} {:answer/id #uuid "5553a4af-1906-5ebb-b828-38daa741b83d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712883} {:answer/id #uuid "ad471761-0632-55a5-8ee0-af5ff0a4025f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad471761-0632-55a5-8ee0-af5ff0a4025f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712890} :answer-field/id #uuid "239aa3a4-e9f0-5cc3-8909-af64520d468d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712877}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "957500c8-da71-5970-a3fc-26819b4da2c7" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=x\\sec y+x^4y$, evaluate $f_y\\left(\\sqrt{2},-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $x^4$ as constant factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_y(x,y)&=x\\frac{d}{dy}(\\sec y)+x^4\\frac{d}{dy}(y)\\\\\n&=x\\sec y\\tan y+x^4.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the given point, the exact values are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sec\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)&=\\sqrt{2},\\\\\n\\tan\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)&=-1,\\\\\n(\\sqrt{2})^4&=4.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute these into the derivative and combine the two contributions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_y\\left(\\sqrt{2},-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\n&=\\sqrt{2}\\cdot\\sqrt{2}\\cdot(-1)+4\\\\\n&=-2+4\\\\\n&=2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8135746b-d411-5521-afa9-2f3bcce86a75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{\\ln(2xyh)-\\ln(2xy)}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712901} {:answer/id #uuid "c1feea51-37de-5457-8449-66c93dd84083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{\\ln\\bigl(2x(y+h)\\bigr)-\\ln(2xy)}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712904} {:answer/id #uuid "cd5635bf-af9e-53ed-9889-61789338d85b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{\\ln(2xy+h)-\\ln(2xy)}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712906} {:answer/id #uuid "da22462b-1583-5015-a1f9-e1dae2231898" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{\\ln(2(x+h)(y+h))-\\ln(2xy)}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712908} {:answer/id #uuid "fd1ea7cd-74ba-52ac-82a5-b88040c9a46f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{\\ln(2(x+h)y)-\\ln(2xy)}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1feea51-37de-5457-8449-66c93dd84083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{\\ln\\bigl(2x(y+h)\\bigr)-\\ln(2xy)}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712904} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9671b9b-d5f9-5bde-a685-91ea5e3bfc3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7a629c31-df5f-5bd8-88c8-f5778f18dba2" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=\\ln(2xy)$ on the domain $xy>0,$ which limit of a difference quotient represents $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$?" :question/worked-solution "For the partial derivative with respect to $y,$ hold $x$ constant and use\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(x,y+h)-f(x,y)}{h}.\n$$\n\nReplace the whole input $y$ by $y+h$ inside the logarithm:\n\n$$\nf(x,y+h)=\\ln\\bigl(2x(y+h)\\bigr).\n$$\n\nThe factor $2x$ still multiplies the incremented input. Thus the logarithm's argument is $2xy+2xh,$ not $2xy+h.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{\\ln\\bigl(2x(y+h)\\bigr)-\\ln(2xy)}{h}.\n$$\n\nHere $x$ is fixed and $h\\ne 0$ before taking the limit. Since $xy>0,$ sufficiently small increments keep the logarithm defined."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712902 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d57ae5c-15cd-5a7d-bcc7-7bf79cc712ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(\\frac{xy+y^2}{x+2y}-\\frac{x(y+h)+(y+h)^2}{x+2(y+h)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712893} {:answer/id #uuid "4ac9ba03-70b3-5581-8551-51d35af0fb5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(\\frac{x(y+h)+(y+h)^2}{x+2y}-\\frac{xy+y^2}{x+2y}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712896} {:answer/id #uuid "5ccd20c3-e68c-5b57-a436-725b32cce818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(\\frac{x(y+h)+(y+h)^2}{x+2(y+h)}-\\frac{xy+y^2}{x+2y}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712898} {:answer/id #uuid "c678d4f8-92ef-53f5-aa8f-0b411583e176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(\\frac{xy+y^2}{x+2(y+h)}-\\frac{xy+y^2}{x+2y}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712905} {:answer/id #uuid "ddcfeead-523c-5910-9bb1-9a72ecd35824" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(\\frac{(x+h)(y+h)+(y+h)^2}{x+h+2(y+h)}-\\frac{xy+y^2}{x+2y}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ccd20c3-e68c-5b57-a436-725b32cce818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(\\frac{x(y+h)+(y+h)^2}{x+2(y+h)}-\\frac{xy+y^2}{x+2y}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712898} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f35bfdb-02e0-51c5-a9ed-5c8174927b42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712903}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8ce7a70c-484e-561e-b846-c96b367f5a49" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=\\dfrac{xy+y^2}{x+2y}$ on the domain $x+2y\\ne 0,$ which limit of a difference quotient represents $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$?" :question/worked-solution "Hold $x$ constant. The definition requires\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(x,y+h)-f(x,y)}{h}.\n$$\n\nEvery occurrence of $y$ in the incremented function value must change: the $y$ in $xy,$ the input being squared, and the $y$ in the denominator. Hence\n\n$$\nf(x,y+h)=\\frac{x(y+h)+(y+h)^2}{x+2(y+h)}.\n$$\n\nSubtract the entire original fraction and divide the difference by $h$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(\\frac{x(y+h)+(y+h)^2}{x+2(y+h)}-\\frac{xy+y^2}{x+2y}\\right).\n$$\n\nChanging only the numerator or only the denominator does not give $f(x,y+h).$ Changing $x$ as well would also violate the definition. Here $h\\ne 0$ before taking the limit; $x+2y\\ne 0$ ensures that sufficiently small increments keep both function values defined."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712911 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b57783c-8def-533f-8483-c7544ea843af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{2(x+h)y^2+2xy^2}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712892} {:answer/id #uuid "31ffcd9c-149f-5b61-89cd-89fd658e170b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{2(x+h)(y+h)^2-2xy^2}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712895} {:answer/id #uuid "5abbc785-140a-5d93-9a52-f6eed4cb7478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{2(x+h)y^2-2xy^2}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712897} {:answer/id #uuid "7f5bbe87-8036-5e10-8eee-49164fe6e880" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{2xy^2-2(x+h)y^2}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712900} {:answer/id #uuid "cdfa091f-dc4b-581d-bb4e-bc17823da408" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{2x(y+h)^2-2xy^2}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5abbc785-140a-5d93-9a52-f6eed4cb7478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{2(x+h)y^2-2xy^2}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712897} :answer-field/id #uuid "3165cd95-19f1-5d21-a4d7-1f8fb553ff13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712894}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "eafd04ef-e7dc-56f3-a7c9-b30740b6352f" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=2xy^2,$ which limit of a difference quotient represents $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$?" :question/worked-solution "For the partial derivative with respect to $x,$ hold $y$ constant and use\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x+h$ for $x$ gives\n\n$$\nf(x+h,y)=2(x+h)y^2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{2(x+h)y^2-2xy^2}{h}.\n$$\n\nOnly the $x$ coordinate changes. The numerator subtracts the original function value from the incremented value, and $h\\ne 0$ before taking the limit."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713064 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1155411d-5f9c-5e6f-8706-5171f919f32b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6e^{3x+2y}+4xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713063} {:answer/id #uuid "546a68e7-1412-51c1-8974-d345b92f3b77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3x+2y}+2xy^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713067} {:answer/id #uuid "6283f21b-d0db-59e8-b6e9-f56a327d1a64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e^{3x+2y}+2xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713069} {:answer/id #uuid "89007c04-0eb2-54c1-83cc-ff69c6d279b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e^{3x+2y}+2xy^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713071} {:answer/id #uuid "e3128806-3813-574f-bef2-c1d6b0bafa26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{3x+2y}+2x^2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89007c04-0eb2-54c1-83cc-ff69c6d279b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e^{3x+2y}+2xy^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713071} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd63d4bc-902f-5188-8650-967690a75fa6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713080}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1783fd66-9c6d-50c1-b707-f17924761eb3" :question/problem "Find $f_x(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=e^{3x+2y}+x^2y^2.$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $f_x$ means the partial derivative with respect to $x$. Hold $y$ constant, so $e^{2y}$ and $y^2$ are constant multipliers. First write $e^{3x+2y}=e^{2y}e^{3x}$.\n\nUsing the sum and constant multiple rules,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x(x,y)\n&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(e^{2y}e^{3x})+\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(x^2y^2) \\\\\n&=e^{2y}\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(e^{3x})+y^2\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(x^2) \\\\\n&=e^{2y}\\cdot 3e^{3x}+y^2\\cdot 2x \\\\\n&=3e^{3x+2y}+2xy^2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe factor $3$ comes from differentiating $e^{3x}$; the held factor $e^{2y}$ is unchanged."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713066 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04215ebb-fd67-5b0c-a30d-5c56c5cc575d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{y}+\\ln x+e^{2x+y}+\\frac{x}{y^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713062} {:answer/id #uuid "1c66bc44-d6c5-5e11-97e9-31f576b83c68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{y}+\\ln x+2e^{2x+y}-\\frac{x}{y^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713065} {:answer/id #uuid "96cd781e-c908-5dfb-98fa-7c6e1c373304" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln y+\\frac{y}{x}+2e^{2x+y}+\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713074} {:answer/id #uuid "b49462cd-7fe4-5da1-a83c-fd4a7fd5798d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{y}+\\ln x+e^{2x+y}-\\frac{x}{y^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713077} {:answer/id #uuid "d35d20c4-144e-5618-9c8d-0c6716520ca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{y}{x}+e^{2x+y}-\\frac{x}{y^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b49462cd-7fe4-5da1-a83c-fd4a7fd5798d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{y}+\\ln x+e^{2x+y}-\\frac{x}{y^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713077} :answer-field/id #uuid "e12667bc-561a-5eba-b132-c79b2a0c0b00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713081}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "460eff50-09be-55c7-8f8c-66579465ed1e" :question/problem "Find $f_y(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=x\\ln y+y\\ln x+e^{2x+y}+\\dfrac{x}{y}$, where $x>0$ and $y>0$." :question/worked-solution "The notation $f_y$ means the partial derivative with respect to $y$. Treat $x$ as constant throughout. In particular, $\\ln x$ is a constant multiplier in $y\\ln x$, whereas $\\ln y$ must be differentiated in $x\\ln y$.\n\nRewrite $e^{2x+y}=e^{2x}e^y$ and $x/y=xy^{-1}$ to expose the constant multipliers. Apply the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_y(x,y)\n&=x\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(\\ln y)\n  +\\ln x\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(y) \\\\\n&\\quad +e^{2x}\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(e^y)\n  +x\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(y^{-1}) \\\\\n&=x\\cdot\\frac{1}{y}+\\ln x\\cdot 1+e^{2x}\\cdot e^y+x\\cdot(-y^{-2}) \\\\\n&=\\frac{x}{y}+\\ln x+e^{2x+y}-\\frac{x}{y^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nHere $x$ survives as a multiplier in the first and last terms. The last term is negative because the derivative of $y^{-1}$ is $-y^{-2}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713068 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72f4ae8f-a5a0-58c1-96b1-dc0a8f2462e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\cos y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713070} {:answer/id #uuid "8b9267be-1edf-5cbd-af6c-d393468fc1e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\cos y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713072} {:answer/id #uuid "9a0deecd-81e7-53e2-97af-c5d91f02dd80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\cos y+y^3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713075} {:answer/id #uuid "a24847d6-cde7-54ca-b25a-e1bae711db1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\cos y+3y^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713076} {:answer/id #uuid "d0a729a7-6435-5b5d-afac-e8d1f9bf40f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x^2\\sin y+3y^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713078}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b9267be-1edf-5cbd-af6c-d393468fc1e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\cos y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713072} :answer-field/id #uuid "92d97d99-5074-5b41-870a-058fe32ff724" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5648ee7f-e590-5b9b-9ead-ed028a8ff682" :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ given that $f(x,y)=x^2\\cos y+y^3.$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiate with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant. Thus $\\cos y$ is a constant multiplier, and the entire term $y^3$ is constant.\n\nUsing the sum and constant multiple rules,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\n&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(x^2\\cos y)+\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(y^3) \\\\\n&=\\cos y\\cdot\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(x^2)+0 \\\\\n&=\\cos y\\cdot 2x+0 \\\\\n&=2x\\cos y.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713285 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "171aa759-12ab-5c4d-b2b7-5e4d03ffffeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{(x+h)y+3y^2-\\left(xy+3y^2\\right)}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713283} {:answer/id #uuid "57c7322d-c1fa-5e5a-b046-0aef049816ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{(x+h)(y+h)+3(y+h)^2-\\left(xy+3y^2\\right)}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713289} {:answer/id #uuid "8368c453-fb3d-5b7b-a0b1-152dc7e7e284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{xy+3y^2-\\left((x+h)y+3y^2\\right)}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713298} {:answer/id #uuid "8f218af9-d6f6-5862-8314-43e5517953af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{x(y+h)+3(y+h)^2-\\left(xy+3y^2\\right)}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713301} {:answer/id #uuid "df8b4f46-4efa-5864-8632-942390356351" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{xy+3y^2-\\left(x(y+h)+3(y+h)^2\\right)}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "171aa759-12ab-5c4d-b2b7-5e4d03ffffeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{(x+h)y+3y^2-\\left(xy+3y^2\\right)}{h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713283} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b370940-ccc6-5d39-bba5-887d9b6eb8df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713284}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "23013d9b-ac5b-51bf-8eb2-e2d4f095902f" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=xy+3y^2$, which limit of a difference quotient represents $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$?" :question/worked-solution "Hold $y$ constant. The definition gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}.\n$$\n\nReplace every occurrence of $x$ by $(x+h)$ in the function, preserving each operator and its input:\n\n$$\nf(x+h,y)=(x+h)y+3y^2.\n$$\n\nSubtract the entire original function value and divide by $h$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{(x+h)y+3y^2-\\left(xy+3y^2\\right)}{h}\n$$\n\nOnly $x$ changes, and $h\\ne 0$ before taking the limit."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713292 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a5fc793-1b49-5c4a-825b-61ec79ef944d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(x^{y}-(x+h)^{y}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713290} {:answer/id #uuid "62727de8-29b1-5d08-a3b9-bfc1e64b7597" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(x^{y}-x^{(y+h)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713293} {:answer/id #uuid "63e76760-f795-5799-9d5e-dfc92a87d7a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(x^{(y+h)}-x^{y}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713294} {:answer/id #uuid "80864907-c591-5f4b-b13f-a460d7b95806" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left((x+h)^{y}-x^{y}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713297} {:answer/id #uuid "8d8b65f8-6fd9-5d9c-8669-2e010e66e2fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left((x+h)^{(y+h)}-x^{y}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63e76760-f795-5799-9d5e-dfc92a87d7a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(x^{(y+h)}-x^{y}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713294} :answer-field/id #uuid "bda56432-d74d-5481-bd9d-339fabd5e9c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "622aa492-2779-5cd0-a4bb-4b66328857db" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=x^{y}$ on the domain $x>0$, which limit of a difference quotient represents $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$?" :question/worked-solution "Hold $x$ constant. The definition gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(x,y+h)-f(x,y)}{h}.\n$$\n\nReplace every occurrence of $y$ by $(y+h)$ in the function, preserving each operator and its input:\n\n$$\nf(x,y+h)=x^{(y+h)}.\n$$\n\nSubtract the entire original function value and divide by $h$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(x^{(y+h)}-x^{y}\\right)\n$$\n\nOnly $y$ changes, and $h\\ne 0$ before taking the limit. The stated domain places the inputs in a differentiable interior region; sufficiently small increments keep the function defined."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713302 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "749a5e27-f2ae-5206-9d2f-8728e62fb9c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(x^{3}\\ln((y+h))-x^{3}\\ln(y)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713295} {:answer/id #uuid "a5c7c791-4985-54e8-a827-c2635af661a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left((x+h)^{3}\\ln(y)-x^{3}\\ln(y)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713303} {:answer/id #uuid "b8c73c13-1c60-5360-8d91-ecbb4c68cf26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(x^{3}\\ln(y)-x^{3}\\ln((y+h))\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713306} {:answer/id #uuid "ba75e2fe-1940-5ab2-a08d-bd2230828476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left((x+h)^{3}\\ln((y+h))-x^{3}\\ln(y)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713307} {:answer/id #uuid "e33536ab-825e-5cfc-b29c-6cc010376842" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(x^{3}\\ln(y)-(x+h)^{3}\\ln(y)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "749a5e27-f2ae-5206-9d2f-8728e62fb9c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(x^{3}\\ln((y+h))-x^{3}\\ln(y)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713295} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5a5c0d4-682f-5186-b274-bf2afa9086a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713311}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "989ede62-fb16-5adb-bc3d-2055132d02d0" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=x^{3}\\ln(y)$ on the domain $y>0$, which limit of a difference quotient represents $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$?" :question/worked-solution "Hold $x$ constant. The definition gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(x,y+h)-f(x,y)}{h}.\n$$\n\nReplace every occurrence of $y$ by $(y+h)$ in the function, preserving each operator and its input:\n\n$$\nf(x,y+h)=x^{3}\\ln((y+h)).\n$$\n\nSubtract the entire original function value and divide by $h$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(x^{3}\\ln((y+h))-x^{3}\\ln(y)\\right)\n$$\n\nOnly $y$ changes, and $h\\ne 0$ before taking the limit. The stated domain places the inputs in a differentiable interior region; sufficiently small increments keep the function defined."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713308 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11dbec47-8c55-5254-819f-8ace66591664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(\\cos((x+h)-y^{2})+\\cos(x-y^{2})\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713281} {:answer/id #uuid "3cf2de7a-7ddb-5aab-8bc1-3a541a422444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(\\cos((x+h)-(y+h)^{2})-\\cos(x-y^{2})\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713287} {:answer/id #uuid "549547a0-1f9e-5888-8059-19a18a4855e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(\\cos(x-(y+h)^{2})+\\cos(x-y^{2})\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713288} {:answer/id #uuid "5f6ccdcc-a5db-5acb-875c-f9018fee323f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(\\cos((x+h)-y^{2})-\\cos(x-y^{2})\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713291} {:answer/id #uuid "c856b83a-eeb8-590e-8f14-7764388ab336" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(\\cos(x-(y+h)^{2})-\\cos(x-y^{2})\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f6ccdcc-a5db-5acb-875c-f9018fee323f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(\\cos((x+h)-y^{2})-\\cos(x-y^{2})\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713291} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2463f8d-2cc2-5a60-acbe-fa357d4e3949" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713314}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bc68ecd7-b2cb-5fc0-8b41-c4d62db0731b" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=\\cos(x-y^{2})$, which limit of a difference quotient represents $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$?" :question/worked-solution "Hold $y$ constant. The definition gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}.\n$$\n\nReplace every occurrence of $x$ by $(x+h)$ in the function, preserving each operator and its input:\n\n$$\nf(x+h,y)=\\cos((x+h)-y^{2}).\n$$\n\nSubtract the entire original function value and divide by $h$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(\\cos((x+h)-y^{2})-\\cos(x-y^{2})\\right)\n$$\n\nOnly $x$ changes, and $h\\ne 0$ before taking the limit."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713312 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12b8627d-bc77-5570-a4c2-8fa828a8316f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(\\sin((x+h)y)-\\sin(xy)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713282} {:answer/id #uuid "24c1f1b5-4622-542b-92f1-c44e542d37ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(\\sin((x+h)y)+\\sin(xy)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713286} {:answer/id #uuid "8e9ca34e-662b-5603-933d-5ada5690d2cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(\\sin((x+h)(y+h))-\\sin(xy)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713300} {:answer/id #uuid "ae3e2641-bbd0-5ac5-a2c9-eb25c99d6d65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(\\sin(x(y+h))-\\sin(xy)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713304} {:answer/id #uuid "afc8a4a2-89ab-5f33-8e11-db9efa0da993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(\\sin(x(y+h))+\\sin(xy)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae3e2641-bbd0-5ac5-a2c9-eb25c99d6d65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(\\sin(x(y+h))-\\sin(xy)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713304} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a9b2075-da9d-563d-aa77-830eb4ffd730" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d7ed675c-67bd-51aa-b918-b66e4400d229" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=\\sin(xy)$, which limit of a difference quotient represents $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$?" :question/worked-solution "Hold $x$ constant. The definition gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(x,y+h)-f(x,y)}{h}.\n$$\n\nReplace every occurrence of $y$ by $(y+h)$ in the function, preserving each operator and its input:\n\n$$\nf(x,y+h)=\\sin(x(y+h)).\n$$\n\nSubtract the entire original function value and divide by $h$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{h}\\left(\\sin(x(y+h))-\\sin(xy)\\right)\n$$\n\nOnly $y$ changes, and $h\\ne 0$ before taking the limit."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713484 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "112d9e89-0b8a-575d-b7cb-b7b558f56de1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{y} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713475} {:answer/id #uuid "4763f31a-58fb-5c9d-9a64-cd4c47b3fabd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x e^{y} + e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713481} {:answer/id #uuid "655a2394-f54e-564a-9bb1-b26f1bad49d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{x} + e^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713488} {:answer/id #uuid "b835b96a-7b42-5d01-bdbe-7c4e1f3b1853" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- e^{y} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713499} {:answer/id #uuid "eb834721-92e0-52d4-ab0b-16fe052d0a95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- x e^{y} - e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4763f31a-58fb-5c9d-9a64-cd4c47b3fabd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x e^{y} + e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713481} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6bf43b3-d407-501d-9e18-ad5199114769" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713498}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "51e20725-2c30-5fee-9590-fd43548b6871" :question/problem "Find $f_{y}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=x e^{y}+y e^{x}$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as constant. Apply the sum and constant multiple rules term by term.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x e^{y}) &=x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(e^{y}) \\\\\n&=x\\cdot \\left(e^{y}\\right) \\\\\n&=x e^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y e^{x}) &=e^{x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\\n&=e^{x}\\cdot \\left(1\\right) \\\\\n&=e^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $f_{y}(x,y)=x e^{y} + e^{x}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713485 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34cdaa6c-1dd9-567d-b19a-0ece1a61f140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x e^{y} + e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713477} {:answer/id #uuid "4ef77582-f3a2-5f8d-8c1c-670d9c3b3d7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x e^{y} + y e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713482} {:answer/id #uuid "5bded3cf-11fd-5f24-bf1a-4dd0f539a44e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 x e^{y} - e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713487} {:answer/id #uuid "7228916d-9c0f-554d-8bc3-4a1037f3f108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y e^{x} + 2 e^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713491} {:answer/id #uuid "b0c65c0c-ca47-59e3-9105-65900077dc97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- y e^{x} - 2 e^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7228916d-9c0f-554d-8bc3-4a1037f3f108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y e^{x} + 2 e^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713491} :answer-field/id #uuid "e37feb59-1815-5f89-8772-d2c7a64ac24c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5a5be5b2-6e2a-5f9e-84f8-eebaab60cc90" :question/problem "Find $f_{x}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=2 x e^{y}+y e^{x}$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as constant. Apply the sum and constant multiple rules term by term.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2 x e^{y}) &=2 e^{y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\\n&=2 e^{y}\\cdot \\left(1\\right) \\\\\n&=2 e^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y e^{x}) &=y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(e^{x}) \\\\\n&=y\\cdot \\left(e^{x}\\right) \\\\\n&=y e^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $f_{x}(x,y)=y e^{x} + 2 e^{y}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713492 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f46157e-4d36-56fc-923f-58d011368fcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 x}{\\sqrt{- y^{2} + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713474} {:answer/id #uuid "39507883-9c95-5ce3-bb25-226c4d15c2f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 x}{\\sqrt{- y^{2} + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713478} {:answer/id #uuid "5128d09f-6c8e-5583-b389-dddd3dcd9dbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{- y^{2} + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713483} {:answer/id #uuid "7015f03d-654c-5549-a0c1-fef2d63398c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{- y^{2} + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713490} {:answer/id #uuid "f4bc4e62-81b7-59ea-927f-8b243cf5ef1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{- y^{2} + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39507883-9c95-5ce3-bb25-226c4d15c2f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 x}{\\sqrt{- y^{2} + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713478} :answer-field/id #uuid "90040c04-80f8-56ba-bd11-c30cd747abeb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713494}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7efdb431-97f3-5fe4-9816-97ae8b917488" :question/problem "Find $f_{y}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=3 x \\arcsin{\\left(y \\right)}+3 x^{2}$, where $-1<y<1$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as constant. Apply the sum and constant multiple rules term by term.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3 x \\arcsin{\\left(y \\right)}) &=3 x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\arcsin{\\left(y \\right)}) \\\\\n&=3 x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{- y^{2} + 1}}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\frac{3 x}{\\sqrt{- y^{2} + 1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3 x^{2}) &=3 x^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(1) \\\\\n&=3 x^{2}\\cdot \\left(0\\right) \\\\\n&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $f_{y}(x,y)=\\frac{3 x}{\\sqrt{- y^{2} + 1}}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713500 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ccef1b6-e029-5925-a086-5c560ada47e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 y^{2} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713489} {:answer/id #uuid "8e56ca33-be28-59de-94bf-23c17a2ab35b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 y^{2} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713493} {:answer/id #uuid "d237da93-f746-5b52-9213-d0a3522badb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 e^{x} - \\frac{3 y^{2}}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713501} {:answer/id #uuid "e6b04a78-76f6-5355-96d6-ad52e45c848e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 y^{2} \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} - 2 e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713505} {:answer/id #uuid "ed19aadf-3227-5be8-b498-af8bd9dbd973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 y^{2} \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} + 2 e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713507}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed19aadf-3227-5be8-b498-af8bd9dbd973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 y^{2} \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} + 2 e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713507} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ae5462a-74f6-572d-9946-add2dc9dd7e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c63e8e49-a150-56a8-b628-d55ceebd82c6" :question/problem "Find $f_{y}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=- y^{3} \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}+2 y e^{x}$, where $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as constant. Apply the sum and constant multiple rules term by term.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- y^{3} \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}) &=- \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y^{3}) \\\\\n&=- \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\cdot \\left(3 y^{2}\\right) \\\\\n&=- 3 y^{2} \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2 y e^{x}) &=2 e^{x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\\n&=2 e^{x}\\cdot \\left(1\\right) \\\\\n&=2 e^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $f_{y}(x,y)=- 3 y^{2} \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} + 2 e^{x}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713503 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "195899e8-70a1-5f6a-8d5a-ae70d37f2ace" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 y^{2} - 2 y \\arcsin{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713476} {:answer/id #uuid "3bc82773-2b14-5bbb-97ca-786220a0fd85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 y + 2 \\arcsin{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713479} {:answer/id #uuid "93fcbbd4-e7e3-58a5-8279-812f8ef96075" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2 y}{\\sqrt{- x^{2} + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713495} {:answer/id #uuid "ad69dbda-f5d2-52c9-9431-39fc463c3802" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 y - 2 \\arcsin{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713496} {:answer/id #uuid "d3ac9dc5-5d4d-5095-a9e7-79e11add8cd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 y}{\\sqrt{- x^{2} + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad69dbda-f5d2-52c9-9431-39fc463c3802" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 y - 2 \\arcsin{\\left(x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713496} :answer-field/id #uuid "45e91bad-c3c6-5abb-a85c-0b01b7660df4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d62269e4-b061-5de0-8e0a-cf4f4037af17" :question/problem "Find $f_{y}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=- 2 y \\arcsin{\\left(x \\right)}- 3 y^{2}$, where $-1<x<1$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as constant. Apply the sum and constant multiple rules term by term.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 2 y \\arcsin{\\left(x \\right)}) &=- 2 \\arcsin{\\left(x \\right)}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\\n&=- 2 \\arcsin{\\left(x \\right)}\\cdot \\left(1\\right) \\\\\n&=- 2 \\arcsin{\\left(x \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 3 y^{2}) &=-3\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y^{2}) \\\\\n&=-3\\cdot \\left(2 y\\right) \\\\\n&=- 6 y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $f_{y}(x,y)=- 6 y - 2 \\arcsin{\\left(x \\right)}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713573 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "220093e7-a461-5b2a-8682-00e542189f3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2 + e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713577} {:answer/id #uuid "362b31ee-223c-513c-9554-9413ca96e757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713584} {:answer/id #uuid "43cbf49e-792e-5eef-a89c-230e73d2cbfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713589} {:answer/id #uuid "5d2c5e96-d1b9-53be-b6e3-75e7debfc8ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 + e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713593} {:answer/id #uuid "be719cd8-1090-5075-a416-e2b99b116e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713598}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d2c5e96-d1b9-53be-b6e3-75e7debfc8ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 + e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713593} :answer-field/id #uuid "830b09d1-f6bd-52c8-a965-a029f25a15d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713595}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "099e0544-01a4-5351-9f4b-f28293480bcc" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=e^{x} \\ln{(y )}+2 y x^{5}$, evaluate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$ at the point $(1,1)$." :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(e^{x} \\ln{(y )}+2 y x^{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(e^{x} \\ln{(y )})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2 y x^{5}) \\\\  & =e^{x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\ln{(y )})+2 x^{5}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\  & =e^{x}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{y}\\right)+2 x^{5}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =\\frac{e^{x}}{y}+2 x^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(1,1)} & =\\frac{e^{(1)}}{(1)}+2 (1)^{5} \\\\  & =2 + e\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713588 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13cb6587-709d-58d4-8c35-3c964c49fdd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 - \\frac{e^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713575} {:answer/id #uuid "27f1c4d3-2577-5e65-b829-cfc119e6361f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{2}}{2} + 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713581} {:answer/id #uuid "4796747b-9d78-50ce-a83f-648f226b3d8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713590} {:answer/id #uuid "d148f018-b38a-55d6-8339-7dc6c05fb3f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713600} {:answer/id #uuid "f8066404-805d-5092-90a0-d52cc65aa766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{2}}{2} + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27f1c4d3-2577-5e65-b829-cfc119e6361f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{2}}{2} + 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713581} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a46d369-f891-5368-a7cf-81f7909c6d45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713587}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3ec62fc4-7aca-5cde-bae7-34335042abde" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=y^{4} \\ln{(x )}+\\sqrt{y} x$, evaluate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$ at the point $(e^{2},1)$." :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y^{4} \\ln{(x )}+\\sqrt{y} x) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y^{4} \\ln{(x )})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{y} x) \\\\  & =\\ln{(x )}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y^{4})+x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\ln{(x )}\\cdot (4 y^{3})+x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{y}}\\right) \\\\  & =4 y^{3} \\ln{(x )}+\\frac{x}{2 \\sqrt{y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(e^{2},1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(e^{2},1)} & =4 (1)^{3} \\ln{(e^{2})}+\\frac{(e^{2})}{2 \\sqrt{(1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{e^{2}}{2} + 8\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713599 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2357388b-1c0a-5418-8583-7690efc9203e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713578} {:answer/id #uuid "350cab05-11d6-5690-b2e1-999dd505e7b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713583} {:answer/id #uuid "397aa157-380f-5e68-a2e8-50e0c3f46dbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713586} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a28110-035a-5e87-80ab-5e6d8984abad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713597} {:answer/id #uuid "e2ac340a-9749-5ef5-8f72-aff73eb50f9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713602}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9a28110-035a-5e87-80ab-5e6d8984abad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713597} :answer-field/id #uuid "267809e4-876e-5a5a-8c1e-e415b4743636" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c9edc195-823a-5c2e-ac4b-ba7ca607ff90" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=4 y^{2} \\sqrt{x}+\\frac{x}{y}$, evaluate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$ at the point $(1,1)$." :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4 y^{2} \\sqrt{x}+\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4 y^{2} \\sqrt{x}+x{y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4 y^{2} \\sqrt{x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =4 \\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y^{2})+x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =4 \\sqrt{x}\\cdot (2 y)+x\\cdot (-{y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =8 y \\sqrt{x}-x{y}^{-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(1,1)} & =8 (1) \\sqrt{(1)}-(1){(1)}^{-2} \\\\  & =8-(1) \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713601 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a500e4e-9397-59ff-a942-fafcfbf25879" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713574} {:answer/id #uuid "200d9ced-4a51-555c-8ee2-a3686764f729" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713576} {:answer/id #uuid "38186fba-8a54-5694-bce9-ce3720e1c6db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 