 [{:answer/id #uuid "26fdd424-f0d6-5c5a-875e-ec5e83e5cc69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2} + \\frac{6}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713580} {:answer/id #uuid "286eb541-0a80-5a89-abdf-e55cf252483e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{6}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713582} {:answer/id #uuid "490d67da-3cf7-5576-83a1-7a72b81fe931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2} - \\frac{6}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713591} {:answer/id #uuid "5e33bb59-29f4-5885-abf1-74c34d98c754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2} - 2 \\ln{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713594} {:answer/id #uuid "ee36c59a-85cb-516f-836c-3411fbc55ae2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{6}{\\pi} + \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "490d67da-3cf7-5576-83a1-7a72b81fe931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2} - \\frac{6}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713591} :answer-field/id #uuid "e93aa025-9f60-584a-82b4-f55ed4aa2d66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713603}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fff0c50f-8039-5b75-8c50-72eec2dabcc5" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=2 \\ln{(x )} \\cos{(y )}-3 y \\sin{(x )}$, evaluate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ at the point $(\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\pi)$." :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2 \\ln{(x )} \\cos{(y )}-3 y \\sin{(x )}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2 \\ln{(x )} \\cos{(y )})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3 y \\sin{(x )}) \\\\  & =2 \\cos{(y )}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\ln{(x )})-3 y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sin{(x )}) \\\\  & =2 \\cos{(y )}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)-3 y\\cdot (\\cos{(x )}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2 \\cos{(y )}}{x}-3 y \\cos{(x )}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\pi):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\pi)} & =\\frac{2 \\cos{(\\pi)}}{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)}-3 (\\pi) \\cos{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)} \\\\  & =- \\frac{6}{\\pi}-\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2} - \\frac{6}{\\pi}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
